{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `Y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the model-block sampling statements so every parameter is sampled from its built-in prior before it is used. In particular, the hyper-priors for `gamma`, `sigma_Sigma`, and `L_Sigma` now precede the `alpha` prior, and all parameter priors precede construction of `Ymu` and the protected-data likelihood. The likelihood for `Y` remains a single top-level built-in sampling statement. `data_safe.json` is unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"/**
 * Schools: ranking school examination resutls using 
 * http://www.openbugs.info/Examples/Schools.html
 */
data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> M;
  vector[N] LRT;
  array[N] int school;
  array[N, 3] int School_denom;
  array[N, 2] int School_gender;
  array[N, 2] int VR;
  array[N] real Y;
  array[N] int Gender;
  cov_matrix[3] R;
}
parameters {
  array[8] real beta;
  real theta;
  real phi;
  array[M] vector[3] alpha;
  vector[3] gamma;
  cholesky_factor_corr[3] L_Sigma;
  vector<lower=0>[3] sigma_Sigma;
}
model {
  array[N] real Ymu;

  // Priors for fixed effects:
  beta ~ normal(0, 2.5);
  theta ~ normal(0, 2.5);
  phi ~ normal(0, 0.1);

  // Hyper-priors:
  gamma ~ normal(0, 5);
  sigma_Sigma ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);
  L_Sigma ~ lkj_corr_cholesky(3);

  // Priors for random coefficients:
  alpha ~ multi_normal_cholesky(gamma,
                                diag_pre_multiply(sigma_Sigma, L_Sigma));

  for (p in 1 : N) {
    Ymu[p] = alpha[school[p], 1] + alpha[school[p], 2] * LRT[p]
             + alpha[school[p], 3] * VR[p, 1] + beta[1] * LRT[p] * LRT[p]
             + beta[2] * VR[p, 2] + beta[3] * Gender[p]
             + beta[4] * School_gender[p, 1] + beta[5] * School_gender[p, 2]
             + beta[6] * School_denom[p, 1] + beta[7] * School_denom[p, 2]
             + beta[8] * School_denom[p, 3];
  }

  Y ~ normal(Ymu, exp(-0.5 * (theta + phi * LRT)));
}
